# ABP Validation

## Automatic Validation
ABP automatically validates:
- Application service method inputs
- Controller action inputs
- Any class implementing `IValidationEnabled`

## Data Annotations
Use standard data annotations on DTOs:

```csharp
public class CreateBookDto
{
    [Required]
    [StringLength(100)]
    public string Name { get; set; }

    [Range(0, 999.99)]
    public decimal Price { get; set; }
}
```

## Custom Validation with IValidatableObject
```csharp
public class CreateBookDto : IValidatableObject
{
    public IEnumerable<ValidationResult> Validate(ValidationContext validationContext)
    {
        if (Name == Description)
        {
            yield return new ValidationResult(
                "Name and Description cannot be the same!",
                new[] { "Name", "Description" }
            );
        }
    }
}
```

## FluentValidation Integration
Install `Volo.Abp.FluentValidation` and create validators:

```csharp
public class CreateBookDtoValidator : AbstractValidator<CreateBookDto>
{
    public CreateBookDtoValidator()
    {
        RuleFor(x => x.Name).Length(3, 100);
        RuleFor(x => x.Price).GreaterThan(0);
    }
}
```

## Disabling Validation
- Use `[DisableValidation]` attribute on method, class, or property
- Validation errors throw `AbpValidationException` with HTTP 400 status
